 method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414557 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "db70d6b5-5ab8-59da-800f-f701ef4ed346" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414557 #edb/ref 1074 "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 7 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+3z=1 \\\\ 0x+y+z=1 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove this equation from the system. So, our system now consists of just two equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+3z=1 \\\\ y+z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ To do this, we apply the back substitution. \n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+z=1\\,⇒\\,y=1-z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2(1-z)+3z=1\\,⇒\\,x=-1-z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1-z \\\\ y=1-z \\\\ z=z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1-z \\\\ 1-z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
